"""
netui — a curses front-end for NetworkManager, with classic dial-up on top.

Tabs      Wi-Fi · Wired · VPN · Mobile · Dial-up · Devices · Profiles
Layout    list on the left, details on the right; nmcli never runs on the
          UI thread, so the interface stays responsive
Manage    connect, disconnect, rescan, hidden SSIDs, forget, hotspot,
          clone, export, reapply changes to a live connection
Create    VPN (PPTP, L2TP/IPsec, OpenVPN, WireGuard, OpenConnect, vpnc,
          SSTP, Fortinet), GSM, CDMA, PPPoE, wired, wvdial dial-up
Tune      IPv4, IPv6, proxy (per-connection PAC and system-wide env),
          routes, DNS, MTU, cloned MAC, metered, firewall zone, priority
Tools     diagnostics (route/ping/DNS), connectivity check, Wi-Fi key and
          QR code, event log

Required: Python 3.8+, nmcli.
Optional: mmcli (modem details), wvdial + pppd (dial-up), qrencode (Wi-Fi
QR), firewall-cmd (zone list), ping/ip (diagnostics).

Run:     ./netui.py  [--tab wifi] [--refresh 6] [--no-color] [--version]
Keys:    ?
Config:  ~/.config/netui/netui.conf
"""

